{"identifier":"always_on_call","title":"Always On Call","description":"Story by Kensiger Jones, directed by John Kennedy. Produced by Premiere Hardcastle, St. Louis. 0551 PA8484 Always On Call 033.10;","videoUrl":"https://archive.org/download/always_on_call/always_on_call_512kb.mp4","thumbnailUrl":"https://archive.org/services/img/always_on_call","sourcePageUrl":"https://archive.org/details/always_on_call","durationMs":544001,"level":"B2","topic":"Motion Pictures: Sponsored;Health and Hygiene;Medicine: Public Health","sourceCredit":"Source: Internet Archive — Always On Call","hasCaptions":true,"segments":[{"startMs":22000,"endMs":23001,"text":"🎵 Henry calling."},{"startMs":24001,"endMs":25001,"text":"Badge 1317."},{"startMs":27000,"endMs":27001,"text":"What's that address?"},{"startMs":29000,"endMs":34001,"text":"Wait a minute, I'll write it down. 1708 Elko."},{"startMs":35001,"endMs":36000,"text":"Name is Connie."},{"startMs":37000,"endMs":37001,"text":"Yeah."},{"startMs":38001,"endMs":39000,"text":"Neighbors are worried, huh?"},{"startMs":40000,"endMs":44000,"text":"Okay, I'll check it. 1708, that's the old widow's place."},{"startMs":44001,"endMs":45001,"text":"I'll get right over there."},{"startMs":59000,"endMs":59001,"text":"[...]"},{"startMs":59001,"endMs":60001,"text":"Who is it?"},{"startMs":62000,"endMs":63000,"text":"What do you want?"},{"startMs":63001,"endMs":65001,"text":"Hey, it's Officer Henry, the policeman on the beach."},{"startMs":65001,"endMs":66000,"text":"Can I come in?"},{"startMs":67001,"endMs":69000,"text":"Yes, it's all right."},{"startMs":70000,"endMs":71000,"text":"Come ahead."},{"startMs":72001,"endMs":75001,"text":"All right."},{"startMs":78000,"endMs":78001,"text":"[...]"},{"startMs":78001,"endMs":79000,"text":"What is it, Officer?"},{"startMs":80000,"endMs":82001,"text":"Why, Mrs. Carney, your neighbors have been worried."},{"startMs":83000,"endMs":85001,"text":"You haven't been outside since you get back from the hospital."},{"startMs":86000,"endMs":90000,"text":"And they phoned the district station, and I was notified to check up and see that you were all right."},{"startMs":90001,"endMs":92001,"text":"They shouldn't have bothered you."},{"startMs":93001,"endMs":95000,"text":"There's nothing you can do about it."},{"startMs":96000,"endMs":97001,"text":"About what, Mrs. Carney?"},{"startMs":98001,"endMs":99000,"text":"About me."},{"startMs":100000,"endMs":102001,"text":"I'm tired and I'm ill."},{"startMs":103000,"endMs":105000,"text":"However, I've paid for my room."},{"startMs":105001,"endMs":106001,"text":"I'm not troubling anyone."},{"startMs":107001,"endMs":110001,"text":"Oh, I know that, and I sure don't mean interfere, ma'am."},{"startMs":111001,"endMs":115000,"text":"But I did get the call, and if you're sick, I could get an ambulance for you."},{"startMs":115000,"endMs":116001,"text":"I'm not going back to the hospital."},{"startMs":117000,"endMs":119000,"text":"I'm staying right here in my room."},{"startMs":119001,"endMs":121000,"text":"Easy now, ma'am."},{"startMs":123000,"endMs":125001,"text":"Say, you are sick."},{"startMs":127001,"endMs":130000,"text":"I'm not going to leave here."},{"startMs":130001,"endMs":136001,"text":"Mrs. Carney, if you don't want an ambulance, won't you let me call Social Service at City Hospital?"},{"startMs":137000,"endMs":139000,"text":"They can send a visiting nurse to see you."},{"startMs":140000,"endMs":141000,"text":"A visiting nurse?"},{"startMs":141001,"endMs":143001,"text":"I don't understand."},{"startMs":144001,"endMs":146000,"text":"They're paid through the community chest."},{"startMs":147000,"endMs":148000,"text":"I won't take charity."},{"startMs":149000,"endMs":151000,"text":"Well, you can pay what you're able."},{"startMs":152000,"endMs":159000,"text":"But, you know, as long as I've been around this neighborhood, I've heard about your doing nice things for people."},{"startMs":160000,"endMs":162001,"text":"Maybe it's time someone did something for you."},{"startMs":163001,"endMs":169000,"text":"Well, I have no family, no one who really cares."},{"startMs":170000,"endMs":173000,"text":"Oh, Mrs. Carney, there are a lot of folks who care."},{"startMs":174001,"endMs":177001,"text":"The people who give one day's pay to the community chest."},{"startMs":178001,"endMs":182000,"text":"They put up that money to help folks just like you here in our own hometown."},{"startMs":183000,"endMs":186000,"text":"And I know what those dollars do, because I see it most every day."},{"startMs":187001,"endMs":189001,"text":"There's a man I help across the street."},{"startMs":190000,"endMs":193000,"text":"He's on his way home from Industrial Aid for the Blind."},{"startMs":193001,"endMs":199001,"text":"He lost his sight some years ago, but thanks to this chest agency, he's still able to earn most of his living."},{"startMs":200001,"endMs":203001,"text":"It's wonderful what fine work those sightless folks can do."},{"startMs":204001,"endMs":206001,"text":"And there's my own sister, Amelia."},{"startMs":207000,"endMs":212001,"text":"Every weekday of the world, she takes my nephew, Jimmy, to the Stella Morris Day Nursery out on Union."},{"startMs":213001,"endMs":214001,"text":"Amelia's a widow."},{"startMs":214001,"endMs":219001,"text":"She has to work, and if it wasn't for the day nursery, she'd have no place where she could leave the boy."},{"startMs":220001,"endMs":226000,"text":"It's a fine place for youngsters, games and refreshments, and they learn how to get along with other kids."},{"startMs":227000,"endMs":231001,"text":"Yes, sir, that's a community chest agency that means a lot to a lot of young mothers."},{"startMs":233001,"endMs":240001,"text":"You know, a policeman is called upon to do all kinds of things, and I guess that's why he knows what the community chest means to St. Louis."},{"startMs":241001,"endMs":246000,"text":"I remember a man who was hurt in an accident, and I helped get him to the hospital."},{"startMs":246001,"endMs":248000,"text":"His right arm was paralyzed."},{"startMs":249000,"endMs":251000,"text":"He didn't have much hope of ever working again."},{"startMs":251001,"endMs":256000,"text":"That is, not until he was transferred to the Miriam Hospital out in Webster Groves."},{"startMs":256001,"endMs":263000,"text":"Out there, they have ways of helping people to get their strength back so as they can use their legs and arms."},{"startMs":264000,"endMs":270000,"text":"The men and women who come there are sometimes crippled and helpless, and when they leave, they're ready to return to active lives."},{"startMs":271000,"endMs":275000,"text":"Well, I figured that work like that is worth an awful lot to St. Louis."},{"startMs":276000,"endMs":279001,"text":"The community chest dollars are a mighty fine investment for everybody."},{"startMs":281001,"endMs":291000,"text":"You know, Mrs. Carney, a few years ago, there was a lot of talk about gangs and kids running wild, and I just wonder if people know the other side of the story."},{"startMs":291001,"endMs":296001,"text":"I used to see it every day at the YMCA Youth Center out on Page Boulevard."},{"startMs":297000,"endMs":304001,"text":"That's a place where boys and men can meet and have a good time, and while they're at it, learn something about being good citizens."},{"startMs":305000,"endMs":313000,"text":"Well, they all pay dues, but still without some help from the chest, the place would have to close down, and where would those boys go then?"},{"startMs":314000,"endMs":317000,"text":"For that matter, where would a lot of people go?"},{"startMs":317001,"endMs":321000,"text":"If it weren't for some of the agencies supported by your community chest dollars."},{"startMs":322000,"endMs":325001,"text":"The servicemen who are coming here and asking us, where can we go?"},{"startMs":326000,"endMs":331000,"text":"They're just in town for a few hours between trains or for a weekend pass."},{"startMs":332000,"endMs":343001,"text":"Now, thanks to the success of last year's community chest campaign, we can send them to the USO at Soldier's Memorial, a place to clean up and get passes from"},{"startMs":343001,"endMs":346001,"text":"movies and ballgames and just relax."},{"startMs":348000,"endMs":352001,"text":"We certainly wouldn't be fair to the boys in service if we didn't maintain places like these."},{"startMs":353001,"endMs":358001,"text":"Yes, sir. Where would people turn if it weren't for the red feather agencies?"},{"startMs":359001,"endMs":364000,"text":"Sometimes they find homes for babies whose own parents can't care for them."},{"startMs":364001,"endMs":373000,"text":"That means a new life for the youngster and a new kind of happiness for the parents who give her that foster home until their own folks can take over."},{"startMs":374001,"endMs":385000,"text":"Sometimes that red feather means a decent last few years for an old person with nowhere else to go, a chance to live in peace and dignity."},{"startMs":387000,"endMs":395001,"text":"Like I said, Mrs. Carney, there are a lot of people who care about their neighbors, who want to help them and do help them by giving one day's pay to"},{"startMs":395001,"endMs":397000,"text":"the community chest each year."},{"startMs":398000,"endMs":400001,"text":"You've always been one of those people, haven't you?"},{"startMs":401000,"endMs":408001,"text":"Well, yes. I always gave as much as I was able to. It seemed only right."},{"startMs":408001,"endMs":415001,"text":"It was right. I know, because day in and day out I see what those dollars buy."},{"startMs":417000,"endMs":420001,"text":"Officer Henry, I'm so glad you came to see me."},{"startMs":421001,"endMs":433000,"text":"I guess here in my room alone, I'd forgotten that in this country, in this city, people do care about each other."},{"startMs":434000,"endMs":441000,"text":"I guess you never really know how much the community chest can mean until"},{"startMs":441000,"endMs":443000,"text":"you need it."},{"startMs":444000,"endMs":452000,"text":"You who give one day's pay to the greater St. Louis community chest will walk with that visiting nurse."},{"startMs":453000,"endMs":465000,"text":"You'll be with her not only when she comes to care for me, but in all the homes, where she's truly an angel of mercy, bringing special skill and care to"},{"startMs":465000,"endMs":466001,"text":"those who need it."},{"startMs":467000,"endMs":471001,"text":"You'll give youngsters sunshine and fresh air at summer camps."},{"startMs":472000,"endMs":481001,"text":"You'll give the blind and the handicapped a chance at employment and a real right to the self-respect that comes with self-support."},{"startMs":482000,"endMs":489000,"text":"You'll make old age an easier time for many folks and give youth a sense of"},{"startMs":489000,"endMs":490001,"text":"really belonging to the community."},{"startMs":492000,"endMs":499000,"text":"You'll find homes for homeless infants and extend a welcome to servicemen who are"},{"startMs":499000,"endMs":501000,"text":"a long way from their own towns."},{"startMs":502001,"endMs":510000,"text":"Yes, we who come to need the community chest agencies learn that they're always on call."},{"startMs":510001,"endMs":516001,"text":"That the services they perform are worth far, far more than what they cost."},{"startMs":517001,"endMs":521001,"text":"We know that you do give best through community chest."},{"startMs":522001,"endMs":527000,"text":"So please, give the best you can."},{"startMs":543001,"endMs":544001,"text":"www.cst.eu.com"}]}